# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
dist/
build/

# Test / lint / type / benchmark caches (generated at runtime)
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
# The PARALLEL-mode fragments, which the bare `.coverage` pattern does not match:
# coverage.py writes `.coverage.<host>.<pid>.<random>` per worker and combines
# them afterwards. Measured 2026-09-05: 1893 of them were committed by three
# `git add -A` calls made while a coverage run was in flight, and they would have
# ridden into the promotion PR as 1893 junk files.
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.benchmarks/

# Architecture-audit + dependency-graph artifacts (generated)
architect-output/
skills/**/scripts.svg

# Marketing kit (local only, not versioned)
docs/marketing/

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local overrides
settings.local.json
*.local.md

# Session artifacts (generated at runtime, consumer-specific)
.active_plan
.compaction-snapshots/
.attestations/
cross-validation-output/
deadcode-output/
# Claude Code runtime dir of THIS repo acting as its own consumer
# (the shipped config lives in settings.json / settings.plugin.json at the root)
.claude/

# Study material, kept local (not part of the shipped cycle)
specs/

# Nested repository with its own remote — never a submodule of the cycle
codex-plugin-cc/

# Run records. Every artifact under here is the output of one execution on one
# machine — plans, implementation logs, reviews, alignment briefs, event streams,
# experiment runs. None of it says anything to whoever clones this repository,
# and committing it puts one machine's history in everyone's diff. The directory
# is scaffolded in each consumer by install.sh; it is never carried in the index.
records/

study-material/**
# The phase-transition stream. Per-session and per-machine by nature: what this
# repository's cycles did here says nothing to whoever clones it, and committing
# it would put one machine's run history in everyone's diff.
# SOP run records: per-run and per-machine, like the phase-event stream. The
# PROCEDURE travels with the kit (records/sops/ stays versioned); what
# one machine did while following it does not.
# Per-agent pipeline output. `/pipeline` writes one directory per item under
# `--output-dir`, holding whatever the agents produced on that run. It is run
# output like every entry above it, and it was the one kind that was not listed:
# nine files from three items reached the index before this line existed.

# Agent run logs (consumer-specific)
!agents/.gitkeep
# EXCEPTION: the README describes the routing MECHANISM, not a domain, and
# install.sh copies it unconditionally. Keeping it ignored made every install
# performed outside this machine start with an empty `.claude/agents/` and a
# broken reference in rules/cycle-maintenance.md. The specialists stay out: each
# describes the repos of ONE ecosystem, and it is the project that derives its
# own. The eight the kit carried were removed on 2026-08-26 — they lived here for
# ages without ever being tracked, which is how a flag (--with-domain-agents)
# could deliver files that existed on one machine only.
!agents/README.md

# A domain specialist describes the repositories of ONE ecosystem. Shipping a
# stranger's makes the routing gate refuse every item a consumer files — measured on
# an adopter 2026-08-18: 88 items with real `file:line` evidence, all
# `BLOCKER/unroutable_repo`. So `agents/` is ignored by default and the kit's own are
# excepted by name.
#
# This paragraph existed for days with NO RULE UNDER IT. The comment explained why the
# four were an exception to an ignore that was never written, so any specialist
# scaffolded into `agents/` was tracked, stageable, and one `git add -A` away from
# shipping to every consumer — the precise failure the paragraph describes as
# prevented. A contract whose mechanism is missing reads as enforced, which is worse
# than an absent rule: nobody goes looking.
agents/*.md
!agents/README.md

# The kit's own five — the squad. They are mechanism, not domain specialists: each
# describes a DECISION, not a repository, and makes no claim about any consumer's
# topology. That is the whole reason they may be versioned here when a specialist may
# not. `squad_lead.py` invokes the facilitator through `claude -p` when the mechanical
# selector has no answer, and an agent that is not versioned reaches nobody.
#
# This list is checked against `mechanisms/distribution/install.sh` by `tests/test_squad_agents.py` —
# three files naming the same five is three chances to drift.
!agents/kairos-product-owner.md
!agents/iris-product-designer.md
!agents/daedalus-tech-lead.md
!agents/hermes-scrum-master.md
!agents/vera-technical-arbiter.md
!agents/nemesis-claim-auditor.md
!agents/argus-pattern-analyst.md
!agents/aesculapius-healer.md
!agents/vigil-sentinel.md
!agents/hecate-intake-triager.md
!agents/eureka-defect-hunter.md
!agents/leonardo-researcher.md
!agents/metis-oracle.md
!agents/clio-historian.md
